<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seneslau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/1247">1247</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seneslau was a Romanian voivode of the mid-13th century, known only from King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bela-iv-of-hungary">Béla IV of Hungary</a>'s charter of 1247 to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a>. The charter left his land, east of the Olt in what became Wallachia, to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanians">Romanians</a> as a tributary of the Hungarian crown, and historians regard it as one of the polities later united in the Principality of Wallachia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seneslau.jpg" alt="Seneslau" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NeimWiki · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1246VOIVODATE.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
